135 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 95 0 R
/E (Electronic Design Automation \(EDA\) tools automate the conversion between these abstraction levels. Given the complexity of modern chips, with millions of logic gates, manual design is simply infeasible. EDA software performs synthesis, placement, routing, timing analysis and verification with unmatched accuracy and speed. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
136 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 95 0 R
/E (Very Large Scale Integration \(VLSI\) is the process of creating an integrated circuit by combining millions to billions of transistors onto a single silicon chip. VLSI design involves multiple abstraction levels: system, algorithmic, register-transfer level \(RTL\), gate level and physical \(layout\) level. Each level is progressively refined until a manufacturable design is achieved. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
