<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (Before synthesis, the RTL must be verified against its specification using testbenches. Open-source simulators like Icarus Verilog and Verilator compile and simulate the RTL, while GTKWave inspects the resulting VCD/FST waveform files to confirm its correct functional behaviour. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
150 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
151 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (Placement determines the precise \(x, y\) coordinates of every standard cell within the core area. This process takes two passes: global placement spreads cells roughly to minimise wirelength and congestion while detailed placement finalises cell positions onto the placement rows. OpenROAD employs the RePlAce analytical placer for this stage. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
152 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (Logicsynthesis converts verified RTL into a gate-level netlist mapped to a specific standard-cell library optimising for area power and timing. Yosys is the primary open-source synthesis tool reading Verilog, performing technology mapping and outputting a netlist ready for physical design. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
