162 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 98 0 R
/E (Once verification is complete, the final layout is exported as a GDSII \(Graphic Data System II\) file. This is the industry standard binary format used by foundries to create the physical masks for chips. Both Magic and KLayout support GDSII stream-out. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
163 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 98 0 R
/E (STAverifies that all timing paths in the design meet setup and hold requirements across process voltage and temperature corners without exhaustive simulation. OpenSTA reads the routed netlist parasitic \(SPEF\) and standard-cell timing libraries \(Liberty\) to report slack on every path and flag any violations. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
164 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 98 0 R
/E (Routing creates the actual metal-layer wires connecting all placed cells according to the netlist. This is divided into global routing, which assigns nets to routing regions using tools like FastRoute. Detailed routing then computes the precise geometric wire paths using TritonRoute, while adhering to all design rule constraints. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
