/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 417 0 R
/E (The results confirm that the open-source flow is capable of producing a timing-clean, DRC-clean, and LVS-matchedphysical design without reliance on any proprietary commercial EDA license. Zero timing violations across placement and CTS, along with a fully clean signoff \(0 DRC errors, 0 LVS mismatches, 0 antenna violations\), validate both the correctness of the RTL design and the maturity of the open-source tool ecosystem for practical ASIC implementation at the 130 nm node.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
219 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 418 0 R
/E (This work reinforces that initiatives like Google/SkyWater's open PDK program and the OpenLane/OpenROAD automated flow have substantially lowered the barrier to hands-on silicon design experience for students and researchers, offering a viable, cost-free alternative to commercial suites such as Synopsys and Cadence for educational and small-scale ASIC projects.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
